WEBVTT

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.040
Uh, listen up.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.010
We've got a newcomer today.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.240
Hey! You can enter.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:21.420
Name's Ido.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.100
Stuff happened, and he ended up here.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.390
You must've already heard about it.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:29.590
The rumors about a blue I-machine that extracted Orichalt

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:33.550
from a planet engulfed in a level 4 storm in the Deneb System.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.340
I see, so you're quite the talented one.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.940
Karla Milla-Foden

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.040
In charge of information and sales.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:40.790
Pleased to meet you.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:42.830
My name's Rick Ayer.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:47.300
The first person to ever win the Asteroid Speed 3 times in a row, a speed star!

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.820
I'll have to warn you in advance.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:49.690
Hm?

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:54.780
If you ever get into an accident and I deem your rescue impossible,

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:57.440
I'll abandon you without a second thought.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.810
Woah, this guy is looking
for a fight right away.

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:03.240
And if it's the other way around?

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.390
Obviously, abandon me right away.

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:18.970
Ido!

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:56.990
What?

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:59.160
Ido got swallowed by that rock?

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.790
Little lady and Alice are with him too.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:02.160
Even Maya?

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.080
Rick, where's that rock?

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.490
I'm following it!

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:06.840
Imminent gravity wave located.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:09.010
It's going to Miguel Out!

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:11.300
I locked onto Rick's location.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:16.780
Okay, from this distance it should be possible.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:17.700
Karla?

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.210
Are the mining preparations ready?

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:20.240
We're shooting it out!

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.820
But in these conditions-

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:22.720
I will go.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:23.940
Amanza!

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:28.580
We've got two choices.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.320
Either chase after Ido, or...

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:33.450
Abandon me right away.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:37.120
Just what are our odds?

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.170
Lieutenant!

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.680
We're going right into the warp zone.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:51.510
Hey, hey! Seriously?!

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:54.180
Mattsun entered the warp zone.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.140
Target performed a Miguel Out!

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.020
With Rick and the rest of them!

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:01.060
Dammit!

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:02.940
We're warping out as well!
Hurry up!

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:14.680
We're out in normal space.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:18.080
Kind of went with the flow here,
so what do we do now?

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:19.750
Dig that guy up.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:21.110
You're an excavator, right?

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:22.940
Don't ask for the impossible!

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:24.650
We should wait for Stulti to-

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:25.900
What a dull man.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.000
What?

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.390
Mikuri Maya's life support systems...

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.610
can only work for so long.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.010
Ugh...

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:49.300
Wanna go over the material in
the lecture later today?

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:54.690
You're going to a place like that?

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.610
What is this?

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.550
Something feels wrong.

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.950
It's not like I don't have any friends.

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:18.480
Even if just on the surface,
I think I'm doing well enough.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:22.340
But something just feels wrong.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:26.250
This isn't... my place.

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:27.890
Maya, wake up!

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:29.980
Wake up, Maya!

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:36.450
M-Mr. Ido!

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:38.790
Alice!

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:42.190
Don't worry, her vital signs are normal

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:47.620
Thank goodness.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.620
What is this?

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.340
Where are we?

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:55.670
Inside the rock that assaulted us.

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:57.680
We got eaten?

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.800
No way, we have to get out and fast!

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.220
If we can do that at all.

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:02.220
Huh?

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:03.270
Take a look.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:08.480
The bedrock structure is rapidly changing
and enclosing us completely.

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:12.020
Without a mining rig,
there's no way we can escape.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:16.740
Moreover, because of the intensely
magnetic minerals the comms are down.

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:18.610
We can't even find out what's
happening outside.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:21.240
Surrounding environment,
survival chances...

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:24.660
The space suit life support system,
counting the reserves...

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.340
112 minutes left?

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:28.660
We have to escape in under two hours!

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:34.590
Alice's surrounded by a self-repairing crystal film that's forming an airtight layer.

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:37.590
You could try putting at least
your face inside it.

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:38.780
Wait a bit!

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:41.540
Do you have the gravity wave data on it?

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:42.290
Yeah.

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:52.900
So Alice really is warping the carbon
dioxide out and warping oxygen in.

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:56.960
But based on the numbers, her oxygen supply is steadily going down as well.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:00.850
At this rate, it will be hard for
her to survive as well...

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:02.180
How long will she last?

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:05.480
Based on the numbers, 3 hours or so.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:07.670
I can't lose Alice.

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:09.490
We have to escape in less than 3 hours.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.250
What about me?

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:12.790
Let's look into that.

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:14.190
That?

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:17.840
Looks like it got caught the
same way we did.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.510
A probe? Pretty old too.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:27.930
Is it really alright to get this close?

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:30.350
You can't dig if you don't get up close, right?

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:38.280
Although, it's weirdly quiet.

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:43.510
Just keep calm like this, little rock...

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:00.620
Well, I'll be going now.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:02.380
Tell me what you see.

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:03.570
Right...

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:16.730
The ship interior looks pretty old.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:22.240
It appears to be a 20-year old manned probe for Miguel Net maintenance.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:24.860
The logs say it was on its way
to the Deneb System-

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:25.950
That doesn't matter.

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:27.990
How are the life support systems?

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:28.620
Will they work?

00:08:28.890 --> 00:08:30.270
Doesn't look like it.

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:32.590
The reserve oxygen tank is empty too.

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:34.290
Retrieve the ship's log then.

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:36.500
We might be able to get some info out of it.

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:38.680
Head for the control room.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:50.920
Hey, Alice!

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:52.520
Where are you going! Stop!

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:03.490
The control room, this must be it.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:05.990
Alice?

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:08.480
Wait! You can't just enter!

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.660
Hey, Alice!

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:21.840
Calm down!

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:22.590
Calm down, I said!

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:24.580
It's not giving off any life signs!

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:25.640
It's just a corpse.

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:27.190
But!..

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:29.720
You waste more oxygen by panicking.

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:31.760
Did Alice go there too?

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:34.500
Yeah, she's right here.

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:35.400
Good.

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:37.520
Retrieve the log right away.

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:40.310
G-Got it! I get it, but!

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:42.010
What's wrong?

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:43.810
The place is, well...

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:48.010
I'm going.

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:51.670
Alice, stay there.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:59.400
Huh? It won't budge.

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:02.060
Ugh, no way!

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:03.090
Don't give up!

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:15.980
Got it!

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:24.190
I told you not to waste oxygen!

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:30.040
What are we going to do
without a mining rig?

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:33.450
Mikuri Maya's life support is going to last an hour more at best.

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:35.220
Let's just give up.

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:36.120
You're running away?

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:38.080
Honestly, I'd love to.

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:40.790
But you know, there's still some of it.

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:42.580
Possibility, you know.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:46.960
Approaching this close will
just make it attack you!

00:10:56.470 --> 00:10:59.260
Wait, is he luring the rock formations out?

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.940
He's trying to reduce the
wandering planet's mass!

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:13.290
How is it, Mr. Ido?

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:15.330
I think you should be able to connect.

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:16.770
Yeah, it's okay.

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:18.250
I'll open a monitor.

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:22.140
The majority of it is damaged.

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:24.540
I wonder just how much we'll be able to restore.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:29.730
Sound data, then?

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:30.670
I'll play it.

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:35.300
...0023...

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:38.760
...manned probe Praum...

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:43.540
...by the wandering planet...

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:46.480
...escape impossible...

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:49.020
Is this the voice of someone
who was on that probe?

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.960
	...the reason Raptor stopped...

00:11:53.240 --> 00:12:00.740
...Orichalt was released into space by another civilization with hope of making contact...

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:03.740
...that kind of idealistic thing...

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:06.270
...obstacle...harmful...

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:08.410
...I will move...

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:10.280
...Rajeev retrieved...

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:13.090
...something humanity
should've never touched...

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:16.360
...doctor Arisugawa...

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:19.700
Guess that's it.

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:24.510
Orichalt, obstacle, harmful.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.050
What was this all about?

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:27.420
I don't know either.

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:29.090
There's too little information.

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:31.490
But I understand this much:

00:12:31.490 --> 00:12:35.280
Humanity knew what exactly Orichalt is.

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:38.990
But that truth hasn't been
released even today.

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:42.400
Someone's concealing it
on purpose, but why?

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:46.200
Because Orichalt was essential to
humanity taking a step into space.

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:51.590
But it looks like it had risks comparable to, or maybe even greater than its benefits.

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:55.210
Wandering planet...
That Rajeev thing they mentioned?

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:56.270
Yeah.

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:58.130
If I were to guess...

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:03.640
Humanity already encountered
wandering planets.

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:07.540
They took what looked like aggressive actions towards humans.

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:13.020
The Federation banned jumping into areas that could lead to a possible encounter.

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:18.650
If you think about it, Miguel Net's jagged shape only supports that theory.

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:20.860
No, not just that.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:25.450
The fact they attempted to capture us after we
obtained such a massive amount of Orichalt.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:32.130
The fact Federation's Treaty Compliance agency
approached us and tried forcibly taking us away.

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:38.550
All of that was to conceal the wandering planet's existence and the threat it poses.

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:41.060
You're right, this does make sense.

00:13:41.060 --> 00:13:43.220
And now, the voice recording you just heard.

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:45.180
...obstacle...

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:47.340
...Rajeev retrieved...

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:53.100
If the obstacle is Orichalt, then the wandering
planet's aim must be the same.

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:54.690
Wait a little.

00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:59.320
If your theory is right, then why is the
wandering planet going after Alice-

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:05.700
I'm alright.

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:11.710
I just switched to the last reserve tank,
it got hard to breathe for a second.

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:15.000
Steady your breathing and calm down.

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:20.850
Stulti finished exiting to normal space.

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:23.470
Looks like we shook Observer off.

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:25.490
Clair, confirm our current position.

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:28.890
Karla, use all of the observation
devices you can and find Rick!

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:31.740
The rock that took Ido and the rest
in should be there too.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:33.990
Got it! Fa-Loser

00:14:36.050 --> 00:14:41.650
Don't think we'll let you die that easily, Ido.

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:43.460
Rick!

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:45.150
Are you okay, Rick?

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:46.820
Worried for me?

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:48.660
I sure am happy.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.740
So, lieutenant. How's the Mattsun?

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:53.450
I found it, but as for its usability...

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:54.680
Thought so.

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:59.180
In that case, follow through
with plan B as we intended.

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:01.050
What's the current mass?

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:02.890
Reduced by 22%.

00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:05.660
Total loss is 37% compared to
the initial observation.

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:08.750
Hmm. When it's down by 40%, go for it.

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:09.990
I got it.

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:11.140
Leave it to me.

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:13.270
What's wrong?

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:14.100
Are you alright?

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:15.690
Shit!

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:18.040
There's still some left.

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:19.950
There is, right, Ido?

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:26.660
Shit.

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:28.090
I screwed up.

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:29.870
How could I have?

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:33.870
Guess the legendary speed star
is going to have to retire here.

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:40.880
Ido?

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.840
What happened to abandoning?

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:47.350
I'll do that if there's no possibility

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:51.440
This time the odds were low,
but there was a chance of saving you.

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:52.550
That's why I did this.

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.640
Possibility?

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:54.820
By how much?

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:55.730
7%.

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:58.730
Haha. You're a dumbass.

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:00.860
Is that the thanks I get
for saving you?

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:03.850
As if.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:05.780
Here's where I'll give it back to you.

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:07.200
Your thanks!

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:10.000
Rick, stop pretending to be a cool guy.

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:11.570
Plan B.

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:16.040
The explosion of the mining rig should make the
stream of magnetic fluid break through the rock.

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:23.260
An attack from outside?

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:24.560
Maya, the help's-

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:28.680
Maya!

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:34.270
Did that do it?

00:16:34.270 --> 00:16:35.480
Yes!

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:37.600
No, it's pretty much undamaged.

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:40.020
No holes opened either.

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:41.760
Are you kidding me?

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:43.780
We have to dig with our hands then.

00:16:43.780 --> 00:16:47.490
If we come any closer, it'll attack again.

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:55.900
Mr. Ido, you know, I never had a place to be.

00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:57.610
I always suffered from that.

00:16:57.610 --> 00:16:58.920
What is it now?

00:16:58.920 --> 00:17:02.930
When the captain picked me up,
I thought it was the worst.

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:04.170
Don't talk!

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:07.500
But it's weird.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:14.630
Despite being in such a ridiculous situation,
I kind of think that this might not be that bad.

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:16.630
Are you giving up already?

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:17.680
Mr. Ido...

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:18.980
There's still a chance!

00:17:18.980 --> 00:17:22.400
Alice... Alice...

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:24.570
There's still a chance of survival!

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:33.430
The life support system's past the limit.

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:34.550
Shit!

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:36.920
Is there really no way to save them?

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:38.230
That's...

00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:40.250
There is!

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:42.800
It's too early to give up!

00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:43.960
Pops!

00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:47.800
Good job holding out!

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:49.590
Leave the rest to me!

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:52.640
But the little lady's life support is...

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:54.510
I trust him.

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:56.460
Ido must've done something.

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:57.730
It's not the end yet!

00:17:57.730 --> 00:17:59.270
Get ready, Rick!

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:01.940
Clair! We're breaking through
with Stulti!

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:03.610
Got it! Breakthrough mode!

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:05.400
Rock formations approaching!

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:10.570
Charge right at them!

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:20.830
Guess there's no choice but to use the precious, precious Orichalt then.

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:30.840
Eat this!
Half a year's worth of earnings!

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:42.220
Rick! Fa-Loser!

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:45.060
Retrieve them before the bastard
closes the hole up!

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:47.490
Fa-Loser! Help me out!

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:52.110
Lieutenant Amanza, they'll do it alone.

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:55.660
Ido!

00:18:56.040 --> 00:18:57.280
You're crazy!

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:58.830
I would've abandoned you long ago!

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:01.490
Heh. As if, you liar.

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:16.570
Alice saved her.

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:17.690
However,

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:24.100
once we were out of the magnetic field,
her ability to warp oxygen increased.

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:27.930
It was small, but there was still a chance.

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:30.150
It must've been hard for Alice too.

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:39.490
Well, looks like this job's done.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:40.990
Oops.

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:44.280
Looks like we'll have to run checks on you all.

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:44.660
Huh?

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.760
Looks like the wandering
planet's still after us.

00:19:49.760 --> 00:19:51.860
Persistent bastard!

00:19:51.860 --> 00:19:52.530
Grayman.

00:19:52.530 --> 00:19:53.150
Hm?

00:19:53.150 --> 00:19:57.890
Attach a remote explosive to the Orichalt
we have on board and release it.

00:19:58.050 --> 00:19:59.310
Say what?

00:19:59.310 --> 00:20:02.850
We just threw out half a year's
worth to save you people!

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:05.110
It's targeting the Orichalt.

00:20:05.110 --> 00:20:06.850
I'll explain properly later.

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:10.080
Agh, fine!

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:12.080
I got it, you piece of shit!

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:14.030
That's a massive loss, dammit!

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:34.590
Aaah, what a waste...

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:36.360
What can you do.

00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:38.130
Life's more expensive.

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:44.320
Hm? You not going to Ido?

00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:45.640
You want me to?

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:46.250
Huh?

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:49.250
Wait, did you finally awaken to my charms?

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:50.480
Eh? Eh?

00:20:55.030 --> 00:20:56.000
Fa-Loser.

00:20:56.480 --> 00:21:01.740
My lost past, Alice, the Observer man, wandering planet Rajeev.

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:07.240
I can't help but think these are all connected.

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:10.540
And now there's another clue.

00:21:12.150 --> 00:21:14.050
Doctor Arisugawa.

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:18.130
The name left in that old interstellar ship.

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:20.900
What's the meaning of it?

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:24.270
Searching for that is my...

00:22:58.910 --> 00:23:02.530
Observer's interstellar ship
went missing in action...

00:23:02.820 --> 00:23:06.930
But Sam Taylor's data was supposed to be sent here.

00:23:06.930 --> 00:23:11.830
Chairman Addams, Mr. Hakubi says he has something to talk to you about regarding Dr. Arisugawa.

00:23:12.040 --> 00:23:13.960
I see. I'll go right away.

00:23:15.440 --> 00:23:20.150
So Amatsu Mikaboshi must've
awakened Rajeev again.

00:23:20.800 --> 00:23:23.850
At last I'll...

00:23:26.180 --> 00:23:31.640
That which descended from the tomb that was the wandering planet.

00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:34.650
That which smears ideals and madness.

00:23:34.650 --> 00:23:37.140
That which tries to survive the day and win.

00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:39.900
The desperate struggle stirs
up a reckless wind.
